  "title": "Dataform: Async Workspace Creation & Concurrency Control",
  "summary": "Dataform now offers an asynchronous method for creating workspaces, `createLongRunning`, which requires a `parent` parameter. You can also set a `concurrentActionsLimit` in `InvocationConfig` for finer control over workflow execution.",
  "details": "Developers can now use the `projects.locations.repositories.workspaces.createLongRunning` method to asynchronously create new workspaces, receiving an `Operation` to track its progress. This method mandates the `parent` parameter to specify the repository in the format `projects/*/locations/*/repositories/*`. While the API diff notes this as a breaking change due to the `parent` parameter being strictly required, this only applies to new integrations with this specific method and does not affect existing API usage. Furthermore, the `InvocationConfig` schema gains an optional `concurrentActionsLimit` field, allowing users to define the maximum number of actions that can run simultaneously within an invocation. The `WorkflowInvocationAction` state enum also now includes `QUEUED` to indicate actions awaiting concurrency slots.",
  "impact": "medium",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 8,
